diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index bb03356..102c115 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -251,7 +251,7 @@ sudo mount -a && make down && make up
 | 2 `out_sweep` | the last Sweep Depth mask video |
 | 3 `out_input` | the **init video looped the same way as the render**: while Deforum renders, TouchDesigner's OpenCV writes the exact frames Deforum used (start / stride), at render size, in a codec TD opens, to `td_masks/feeds/input_loop_<key>.mp4` (cached); it plays with the render's playhead and seam crossfade, so outputs 1 and 3 line up frame for frame. This also fixes init videos TD's Movie File In cannot decode (AV1, VP9, HEVC, 10-bit). When the init video is not visible on the share (`td_inputs/comfy_videos` is a symlink Samba does not follow), it is downloaded from ComfyUI's `/view` first; failing that, output 3 is made from the frames Deforum extracted (`<render>/inputframes`) once the render is done |
 
-*Pipeline › Reload Render + Input* loads the last render and its input video again (outputs 1 and 3); with nothing loaded yet it takes the newest render and plans the loop from the current settings.
+*Pipeline › Reload Render + Input + Sweep* loads the last render, its input video and the Sweep Depth video that render used again (outputs 1, 3 and 2); with nothing loaded yet it takes the newest render, plans the loop from the current settings and shows the newest sweep.
 
 ### Snapshots
 
diff --git a/docs/deforum_parameters.md b/docs/deforum_parameters.md
index 435ab89..0051399 100644
--- a/docs/deforum_parameters.md
+++ b/docs/deforum_parameters.md
@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@
 # deforum COMP: parameter reference
 
-Every custom parameter of the `deforum` Base COMP, page by page, as built by `build_master_ui` (tdeforum 0.12.1). **TD name** is the parameter's name in TouchDesigner (`op('deforum').par.<name>`); **default** is the baseline value.
+Every custom parameter of the `deforum` Base COMP, page by page, as built by `build_master_ui` (tdeforum 0.12.3). **TD name** is the parameter's name in TouchDesigner (`op('deforum').par.<name>`); **default** is the baseline value.
 
 Parameters marked **MOD** (their label on the COMP starts with `~`) are the driveable (keyframeable) ones: a float base value plus a `<name>raw` override. Type a Deforum schedule into the raw one (e.g. `0:(1), 30:(1.04)`) and it is sent as written, ignoring the base and any modulation; leave it empty to use the base + CHOP link + Mod Matrix + Mod CHOP.
 
@@ -287,7 +287,7 @@ Units 2 and 3 have their own pages with the same parameters (`Cn2...`, `Feed2...
 | `Loopoffset` | Loop Player Offset (frames) | 0 | Shifts the loop player's start against the timeline. |
 | `Feedloopstart` | Feed: loop start frame (0 = timeline start) | 0 | Timeline frame where TOP feeds and beat_clock start counting (0 = timeline start). |
 | `Feedmethod` | Feed: recording method | addframe | Add Frame: the recorder steps the timeline frame by frame. Continuous: records every cooked frame. |
-| `Reloadoutputs` | Reload Render + Input (outputs 1 and 3) | (button) | Loads the last render (output 1) and its input video (output 3) again; with nothing loaded yet, the newest render with the current settings' loop plan. |
+| `Reloadoutputs` | Reload Render + Input + Sweep (outputs 1-3) | (button) | Loads the last render (output 1), its input video (output 3) and the sweep video it used (output 2) again; with nothing loaded yet, the newest render with the current settings' loop plan and the newest sweep. |
 | `Loopinstart` | Input loop: first video frame | (read-only) | Read-only: first init-video frame the render used (output 3 starts there). |
 | `Loopinstride` | Input loop: video frames per render frame | (read-only) | Read-only: init-video frames per render frame (more than 1 with Video Frame Mode = Stride). |
 | `Loopinrate` | Input loop: render frames per output frame | (read-only) | Read-only: render frames per output frame (0.5 when the render is interpolated x2); keeps output 3 in step with output 1. |
